Subject: Basic string manipulation
Message-ID: <iGhZsAlJF3k.lI63IQxTWswJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/israel-r-user-group/c/iGhZsAlJF3k/m/lI63IQxTWswJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,
I am looking for the "R" equivalent of sscanf.
Basically I something which looks like this: XXX_3_YYY_4 and I want to extract the 3 and 4 while making sure the pattern holds (i.e. ZZZ_4_AAA_5 would not be legal).
The usage would be something like:
a<-c("XXX_3_YYY_4", "XXX_26_YYY_12", "AAA_34_YYY_15");
b<-somefunc(params)
>b
[[1]]
[1] 3 4

[[2]]
[1] 26 12

[[3]]
[1] NA

From ua46587f294177886 at groups.google.com  Sun Jul 21 11:59:23 2013
From: ua46587f294177886 at groups.google.com (Yizhar Toren)
Date: Sun, 21 Jul 2013 11:59:23 +0000
Subject: Re: [Israel RUG] Basic string manipulation
Message-ID: <iGhZsAlJF3k.k3Asp6RoS7QJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <iGhZsAlJF3k.lI63IQxTWswJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
References: <iGhZsAlJF3k.lI63IQxTWswJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/israel-r-user-group/c/iGhZsAlJF3k/m/k3Asp6RoS7QJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Quick and dirty - use two steps:

1. use regular expression to validate your expressions:

x <- sapply(a, grep, pattern = '^XXX_[0-9]{1,2}_YYY_[0-9]{1,2}$', value = TRUE)
a.filter <- a %in% unlist(x)

2. extract what you want:

params <- do.call('rbind', strsplit(a, split = '_'))
params[!a.filter] <- NA
