You can use which

> d
   x  y fac
1  3  1   C
2  3  2   B
3  1  3   A
4  1  4   C
5  1  5   B
6  1  6   B
7  1  7   A
8  1  8   C

9  1  9   A
10 1 10   A

> d[which(d$y>20),]$x = 20

Error in `$<-.data.frame`(`*tmp*`, "x", value = 20) :

  replacement has 1 rows, data has 0

> d[which(d$y>20),"x"] = 20 # does not fail and nothing is updated
> # and to prove that it works
> d[which(d$y>7),"x"]=20
> d
    x  y fac
1   3  1   C
2   3  2   B
3   1  3   A
4   1  4   C
5   1  5   B
6   1  6   B
7   1  7   A
8  20  8   C
9  20  9   A
10 20 10   A

the function "which" returns the indexes the fulfills the condition.
in this case the index 10.

Haki.

2013/7/24 Assaf Mendelson <assaf.m...@gmail.com>

